      "html": "<ul><li>Scientific name: Loricaria cataphracta Linnaeus, 1758</li><li>Common names: L062, Cataphract Whiptail</li><li>IUCN Red List: Least Concern (last assessed 2020)</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1267",
      "html": "<p>South America: Amazon River basin and coastal rivers of the Guianas, including the Lower Amazon (Nhamundá), Guyana, and Suriname coastal rivers (Marowijne). Type locality: mouth of the Marowijne River, near Galibi, Suriname.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1267",
      "html": "<p>Unreported. There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1267",
      "html": "<p>When young, Loricaria spp. can be differentiated from the similar Rineloricaria spp. by their more feathered sucker-mouths. In adults this difference is considerably more evident.</p>"
